James was exploring the appropriate title for a role focused on business opportunities, specifically in the context of building an international academic community of experts. While he initially considered "business developer," I suggested alternatives more suited to academia, such as "partnerships manager," "community engagement specialist," "development officer," "strategic partnerships coordinator," and "director of external relations." These titles emphasize collaboration, securing funding, and expanding programs, aligning with James's vision for a resourceful and strategic approach to community building without the commercial connotations of business development.
